title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1932 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/poultry_catalogue.jpg
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Saskatchewan.

= Inter-Party Relationships

Inter-Party relations are very much a concern in the multi-party politics of Saskatchewan.

[? if fptp = 1 : Despite our First-Past-The-Post system, parties maintain the ability to withhold candidates in certain ridings, endorse another party's candidates, or form a broad United Front. ?]

The Liberals, as the traditionally dominant party, are completely out of the picture when it comes to collaboration. However, the other parties, especially those facing weak polling, may resort to one of the above methods in times of need. 

This is not to mention the possibility of a minority government where collaboration becomes vitally important to ensure a stable government.

- @conservatives: Increase relations with the Conservatives
- @social_credit: Court the Social Credit Party
- @cp_s: Work towards repairing our relationship with the Communists
- @reconstruction: Reach out to the Reconstruction Party
- @new_democracy: Reach out to the New Democracy Movement
- @ccf_ss_alone: The [+ ccf_ss_name +] can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@cp_s
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; cp_s_inter_party_seen += 1
go-to: cp_s_unity if cp_s_unity = 1; cp_s_social_fascism if cp_s_unity = 0

@cp_s_unity
on-arrival: cp_s_relation += 5*(1 - dissent); true_socialist_dissent -= 3; true_socialist_strength += 5; 

The Communists welcome our attempt to reach out to them. 

[? if ccf_ss_unity == 0 : They are hopeful that we will join their Unity Front movement as a broad coalition dedicated to unseating the 'reactionary' dominant Liberals. ?]

@cp_s_social_fascism
on-arrival: cp_s_relation += 2*(1 - dissent); true_socialist_dissent -= 3; true_socialist_strength += 5; 

The Communists are not particularly thrilled that we have chosen to reach out to them. Perhaps Moscow has ordered them not to engage with us?


@social_credit
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; scps_relation += 2 if scps_party_leader == "Needham"
go-to: social_credit_op if scps_in_government = 1 and ccf_ss_in_government = 0 and premier != "Needham"; social_credit_coalition if ccf_ss_in_government = 1 and scps_in_government = 1; social_credit_aberhart if alberta_premier = "Aberhart"

@social_credit_op
on-arrival: scps_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are currently in opposition to the SCPS-led government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@social_credit_coalition
on-arrival: scps_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@social_credit_aberhart
on-arrival: scps_relation += 3*(1 - dissent)

The Social Credit Party of Saskatchewan is deeply intertwined with it's sister party governing Alberta. As it stands, the Alberta Social Credit Party are reluctant to accept our collaboration, given the Alberta CCF's pestering of the Social Credit Movement. Alberta Premier Aberhart, personally offended, has thus been lukewarm at best to cooperation between our parties.

@conservatives
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; lps_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)
go-to: cps_anderson if cps_leader = 'James Anderson' and ccf_ss_name = 'PFLP'; cps_reform if cps_leader = 'John Diefenbaker'; cps_moribund if year > 1940

@cps_anderson
on-arrival: cps_relation += 7*(1 - dissent)

James Anderson is open to cooperation with parties opposed to the Liberals. He welcomes our attempt to increase relations. 

@cps_reform
on-arrival: cps_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

CPS leader John Diefenbaker represents a more populist and reformist angle of the CPS. He recognizes that the party is somewhat diminished and must be able to present new ideas to persist. 

@cps_moribund
on-arrival: cps_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The Conservatives are somewhat electorally moribund, given their reputation as the government that entered the Depression and drought. It seems their role in Saskatchewan politics has ceased altogether. 

@ccf_ss_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

@reconstruction
view-if: 1 == 2

@new_democracy
view-if: 1 == 2

- @return: Continue...
